    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryson Stott** (72.55) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (71.72) anchor the LawDog lineup as our strongest plays. **Bryson Stott** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Buehler, whose 4.56 xERA allows our middle infielder to capitalize on a +13% platoon edge. Meanwhile, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start despite facing a tough arm in Cole; his elite BvP history (+8% score adjustment) and prime spot in the #2 hole maintain his high floor even against elite talent. We are also looking for a breakout performance from **Lawrence Butler** (69.19), who continues to thrive in his platoon split, providing us with a strong secondary source of production while batting 6th against Rea.\n\nThe decision to bench **Gleyber Torres** (49.99) was the most difficult call of the morning, as he hovered just below our target threshold. While his placement in the #1 spot usually provides a boost, his platoon disadvantage against the right-handed Martinez ultimately capped his efficiency, forcing us to prioritize the higher-upside profiles of **Jonathan Aranda** and **Tyler Freeman**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Masyn Winn**; while his 51.23 score is technically marginal, his 59% SB rate makes him a non-negotiable asset given our scarcity mandate, even if the matchup against Gore presents a challenge.\n\nRegarding risk, note that **Tyler Freeman** is currently operating under a \"Lineup Pending\" status; should his projected #2 spot fluctuate, his efficiency score could experience volatility. Furthermore, **Taylor Ward** faces a tricky outing against Tolle; while his 60.28 score is solid, the -10% SP skill impact warns us that this will be a grind. We are maintaining our bench discipline with **Gavin Sheets**, whose 38.57 projection fell well below our 40-point floor, and we continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL.",
